<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgi Dimitrov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1949</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georgi Dimitrov was a Bulgarian Communist leader who won fame in 1933 by defending himself at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> fire trial in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, then headed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-international">Comintern</a> from 1935 to 1943. Returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, he became prime minister in 1946 and established a Stalinist regime, giving his name to the 1947 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dimitrov-constitution">Dimitrov Constitution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georgi-dimitrov.jpg" alt="Georgi Dimitrov" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TASS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgiy_Mihaylovich_Dimitrov_TASS_Portrait_Trim_Edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
